First, I apologize if I am breaking any group rules in my post...I'm
kind of new to posting here.  I'm not sure what the unspoken/spoken
rules here are.  I stopped playing Nethack for about 4~5 years and
started again about 3 weeks ago and finally got another ascension
under my belt.

Standard Valkyrie ascension, with a lot of poorly thought out
decisions toward the end.

Headed straight to the Gnomish Mines, got 2 magic lamps (1 blessed, 1
cursed).  Grabbed my candles then ran back up to Sokoban where I got
an "oR.  Saved my lamps as a light source for a while as I had decent
standard equipment for a while, plus found a [oMP and (oH from a bones
file from my failed wizard.

By the time I found the magic portal to my quest, I still was not high
enough level so I went down to Mines End, grabbed my luckstone and
picked up a touchstone along the way as well.  Finished up the quest,
killed Medusa and began to think more seriously about my wishes.

I had magic resistance and 2 sources of reflection, but I rather like
the convenience of being able to wear "oMB and the security of "oLS,
so I wished for a blessed greased +3 silver dragon scale mail, which I
got...from my 2nd magic lamp.  My first blessed magic lamp contained 1
stingy djinni ;_; So...I have no permanent light source now, so after
I got my /oW from the castle, I got a "brilliant" idea to wish for a
Magic Lamp.

...I remembered shortly after that you cannot wish for "more wishes"
although..I hardly think transfering 1 wish for 1 wish is an abusable
gain :(

...I also remembered shortly after that as well that a high priority
wish from a /oW ought to be ?oC.... hello, /oW (0,0).

I still couldn't complain as I had all of my necessities taken care
of.  I polypiled about 4 times, got a magic marker and got my
excalibur to +7 and fooproofed all my armors.  Luckily I identified a
blessed ?oC, which was used to charge my Marker and write more ?oC.  I
managed to snag another magic lamp along the way to Moloch's Sanctum,
so now I was filled with oodles and oodles of wishes! (more like 3).

Okay here is where things get ugly.

In the Wizard's tower, I encountered my first master mind slayer of
the game.  He sucked my brain and dropped a "new" scroll.  I had
already identified all of the Bad Scrolls, so I carelessly read this
scroll without hesitation... My +7 Excalibur vibrated violently and
then exploded... um, what?

Yeah...I forgot that previously known items (such as ?oEW) can become
unidentified...

Luckily I had a backup +7 Mjolnir...my only other weapon on me... (but
I sorely missed my excalibur)

Things were pretty smooth until the Vibrating Square, or lack there
of.  I spent far too much time trying to find that damn square.  Also
took me 2 rings of the bell of opening to realize something was
wrong...it was cursed.  Finally got the ceremony completed, then
headed up to a frustrating race back to dungeon level 1.

Plane of Earth was fairly uneventful, but I carelessly died in the
plane of Fire to Double Trouble Wizard of Yendor and company... (and I
had 6 blessed !oFH too..) so there goes my only amulet of life
saving.  Another noobie mistake I made was in the plane of Air... same
mistake really.  I picked up a "new" potion... not realy
new...Polymorph :(  Goodbye [oMR, Hello Silver Dragon o.o!  I
rearranged some equipment to use "oR and equip a pair of gray dragon
scales I just found.  Water was uneventful, and I reached...the Astral
Plane.

I really did not think I would make it at this point, as the wizard of
yendor had destroyed 2 pairs of speed boots and other lovely gears I
managed to aquire.  I was at -43 AC prior to entering the elemental
planes....and iirc -24? AC after he destroyed my equipment -_-*

I crossed my fingers, and headed to the right altar, had to kill Death
3 times in the process.  Kiss kiss, it's the right altar! <3
Huzzahhhhhh

So I end the game, learned some good lessons but I still have a
question.  I don't remember Rodney destroying my armor so much in my
previous ascensions, is there something I can do to prevent this?
Perhaps keeping all of my equipment blessed or greased?  He knocked
off 3 or 4 pieces which hurt me pretty badly.  Actually now that I
think about it, I don't think he disintegrated my equipment until I
had lost my [oMR, but then again I had worn gray dragon scales...so
that shouldn't be it either... help :(


